@WeatherVane Apparently that is common for engines designed to produce high torque - tractors etc., and presumably this vehicle too, to have low HP for the CC value. The high torque means you are less likely to get stuck as the wheels will keep putting out a lot of power at low RPM, so you can grind your way out of mud etc rather than spinning your wheels uselessly at high(er) RPM.

